        </div>
        
        <div class="summary-card">
          <p class="summary-text">The foreign exchange market is the largest, most liquid financial market in the world. It operates 24 hours a day, 5 days a week, allowing participants from all time zones to trade currencies. Unlike stock markets, Forex has no central exchange and is completely decentralized.</p>
          
          <p class="summary-text">Currency prices are driven by a complex interplay of interest rates, economic data, geopolitical events, central bank policies, market sentiment, and technical factors. Successful trading requires understanding these drivers and managing risk effectively.</p>
          
          <p class="summary-text">While leverage allows traders to control large positions with small capital, it also magnifies losses. Most retail traders lose money, making risk management the most critical skill to develop. The 1-2% risk per trade rule, proper position sizing, and maintaining a minimum 1:2 risk/reward ratio are essential for long-term survival.</p>
          
          <p class="summary-text">Forex offers unique advantages: high liquidity, low costs, 24/5 accessibility, and the ability to profit in both rising and falling markets. However, it also carries significant risks including broker fraud, gap risk, emotional trading, and the potential for rapid account depletion.</p>
          
          <div class="summary-quote">
            "The goal of a successful trader is to make the best trades, not to be right all the time. Money management and risk control are more important than being right."
